2026-11-01T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2337) 'a garment fit at MESH on the GPU L-BFGS-B
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2337) '- MESH ends with a fit. A garment surface that clips the body is moved out of it by the fit, not by a wider clearance on the strokes (operator, 2026-10-27).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2337) '- The fit follows the intersection-free retargeting fork's start: the body begins shrunk along its vertex normals, so the drawn surface is outside it, and grows back to full size in steps.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2337) '- Each step is one solve by &{repo("contract-lbfgsb")} on the GPU: the shape term keeps the drawn surface's shape, and the IPC barrier keeps every vertex outside the body at that step's size. Every iterate stays intersection-free.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2337) '- The fit runs in the guest of &{repo("interactor-drape")}, which already drives the solver on RenderingDevice and holds the IPC kernels. `drape.elf` comes back to &{repo("transport-meshing-pen")} (operator, 2026-10-27).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2337) '- The pen's check that no garment vertex is inside the body reads the fitted mesh. The scripted skirt's ring clearance goes back to 1 cm, a little more than a pencil's width.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2337) '- RFD66606-2293, which cut the fit from the pen; RFD66606-2294, where compute runs.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2337) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2337) 'Nine of 1910 vertices end up 3 to 12 mm inside the body, from two pennies to nearly a AA battery's width. A 2 cm ring clearance, two AAA batteries side by side, hides it without moving the surface.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2337) 'The solve
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2337) 'For grow fraction `a` from 0 to 1 in `N` steps, the body is `B(a) = B − (1 − a) d0 n`, with `n` the area-weighted vertex normals of the body and `d0` the shrink depth. At each step the solver minimises over the garment vertices `x`:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2337) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2337) 'E(x) = ks * sum over edges (|xi − xj| − lij)^2
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2337) '     + kl * sum over vertices |L x − L x0|^2
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2337) '     + kappa * sum over vertices, candidate triangles of B(a): b(d^2)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2337) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2337) '`lij` and `L x0` are the drawn surface's edge lengths and Laplacian coordinates, and `b` is the IPC log barrier of the drape kernel, zero beyond `dhat`. The step starts from the last step's result.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2337) 'What exists, and what is new
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2337) '- L-BFGS-B on the GPU: contract-lbfgsb `vec_rd`, in the drape guest, run by its solver tests.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2337) '- IPC point-triangle barrier: drape `IpcPointTriangle.lean`, gradient and Hessian, no energy.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2337) '- IPC step bound: drape `IpcStepClamp.lean`, written, not emitted or wired.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2337) '- Shape term and normal shrink: new.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2337) '- Fit entry points in the guest: new. New in the kernels:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2337) '- The barrier's energy, summed per vertex, because a line search compares energies.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2337) '- The step bound inside the line search: the solver's largest step is capped so no vertex moves more than a fraction of its distance to the body. Candidate triangles for each vertex come from the body mesh on the guest's CPU, once per step.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2337) 'Gates and controls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2337) '- No vertex inside: 0 inside, by winding number, after the fit. Control that must fail: the fit off, where the statue skirt has 9 inside.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2337) '- Every iterate outside: 0 inside after every step. Control: the step bound off.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2337) '- The start: 0 inside against the shrunk body. Control: `d0` = 0 on the statue skirt.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2337) '- The shape kept: the move of each vertex is reported. No control, because it is a measurement. Each runs on the scripted skirt (two avatars), the replayed skirt and dress, and the two hand-drawn skirts. The fit runs on RenderingDevice only. The solver's vector ops keep their CPU-against-GPU unit tests.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2337  1 LINE
 Text:Written

